1
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:50,480
Isn't that one of the mangoes
Zheng Yu gave us?

2
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,040
What are you doing?

3
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,440
I was too impatient last time
and ate one too early.

4
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:56,120
It was a bit astringent,

5
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:59,120
so I'm examining it closely
to see if it's ready yet.

6
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:03,120
Someone might think you're going to write
a paper and submit it for publication.

7
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:05,040
Does eating fruit require
the right timing?

8
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:06,400
Of course.

9
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:08,680
It's just like falling in love.

10
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:10,759
If you force it at the wrong time,

11
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:15,040
all your wonderful expectations
will turn into ruin and resentment.

12
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,680
You sound like a love expert.

13
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:19,840
Xu Fangli,

14
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:23,760
the next time I give you fruit,
you had better cherish it like this too.

15
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:44,760
JIANG HAIXING DIGITAL REPAIR

16
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:56,600
What needs fixing?

17
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:02,880
We don't have much. Make do with a bite.

18
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:06,440
What brings you two here?

19
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:09,800
It's hard to get by here.

20
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:13,240
The two of us
even have to keep coming back here.

21
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:15,160
You should know why, right?

22
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,600
In the beginning,

23
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:28,080
it was because she was your niece
that we agreed to lend her money.

24
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:31,680
Otherwise, who would lend
so much money to a kid?

25
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,600
FAST REPAIRS OF PHONES AND DIGITAL DEVICES

26
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:38,080
It's no use telling me this.

27
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:39,000
You…

28
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:45,440
We didn't come to demand money from you.

29
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:47,400
You don't have to be so wary of us.

30
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,240
This city is so big.

31
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:50,680
As her uncle,

32
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:53,040
you must know where she studies.

33
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,800
I… I really don't know.

34
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:01,320
Think about it.
She's a natural freeloader.

35
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:05,840
I avoid her like the plague.
You know that's true.

36
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:10,200
Actually, waiting for her
at her university

37
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,960
is one way to get money.

38
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:16,000
But how much money
could a broke student have?

39
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:17,640
She can't play any tricks.

40
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,800
If you ask me,

41
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,560
let her save some face.

42
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:25,520
She has good grades.

43
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:28,120
She will make bank in the future.

44
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:30,600
Once that happens,
you can get all you want.

45
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:33,080
The food will get cold. Eat.

46
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:36,280
Here.

47
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:59,320
BIOLOGY NOTES

48
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:04,280
What are you looking at?

49
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:07,440
Your tutor really cares about you,

50
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:09,760
even writing notes for you.

51
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:12,040
I paid her, after all.

52
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:16,000
I definitely pay Ms. Zheng
more than the market rate.

53
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,640
What's with that reaction?

54
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:22,680
I envy you.

55
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:26,000
I envy the fact that you can
buy other people's time.

56
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:30,160
And I envy you.
You get my time without spending money.

57
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:36,760
You studied through the lunch hour.

58
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:38,040
No one sat with you.

59
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:41,400
It's sad. That's why I came over.

60
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:44,680
I'll be your study partner for free.

61
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:45,880
Cherish it.

62
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,720
Do you have one of these too?

63
00:05:58,360 --> 00:06:00,160
- Yes.
- Show me.

64
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:02,760
Why?

65
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:05,920
Mine only has biology.

66
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,480
But I want to improve my math.

67
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:09,840
Yours must have a list

68
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,880
of review materials for math, right?

69
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:13,000
Yes.

70
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:22,440
I don't think I brought it. It's at home.

71
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:25,240
Stingy.

72
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:39,640
<i>Laowu. Wu Fa, here's to you.</i>

73
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:44,680
<i>Thank you for not giving me a hard time</i>
<i>over the years.</i>

74
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:48,560
<i>We grew up together.</i>

75
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:50,280
<i>Give you a hard time?</i>

76
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:52,280
<i>You make it sound so terrible.</i>

77
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:13,000
BOOK LIST FOR SCHOOL
1. MUST-BUY, 2. FOR REFERENCE

78
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:28,400
Chen Yanzhou.

79
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:38,160
I sang too much,

80
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:39,960
and my voice turned hoarse.

81
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:40,880
What about you?

82
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:44,720
Did you lose your voice
from that birthday party?

83
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:50,760
Zheng Yu.

84
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:53,720
Zheng Yu.

85
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,160
Fine.

86
00:07:58,760 --> 00:08:00,080
Team building.

87
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:02,240
If you don't talk, I won't talk either.

88
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:12,440
Welcome.

89
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:16,320
Give… Give me a few of these fish balls.

90
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,680
Just a moment.

91
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:23,400
Bro.

92
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:27,080
I think Jiang Haixing is right.

93
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:29,240
She's a broke student.

94
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:32,120
Even if we push her,
where will she get so much money?

95
00:08:33,919 --> 00:08:36,000
Jiang Haixing wouldn't tell us
where she's studying

96
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:39,720
because he's afraid his niece
will turn and ask him for money.

97
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:42,760
Whether he gives it is another matter.

98
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:46,920
Would his adopted son
just leave his biological sister hanging?

99
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:50,360
What else did he say?

100
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,320
She will make bank in the future?

101
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:55,280
What if she finds a job and runs far away?

102
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:56,200
What will we do?

103
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:58,280
Chase her across the world?

104
00:08:58,360 --> 00:08:59,800
You're right.

105
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:03,000
But the university is so big.
Where will we find her?

106
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:05,360
Zheng Yu is good at hiding.

107
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:08,680
No rush. We'll search slowly.

108
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:10,880
She won't be getting away.

109
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:23,560
ZHENG YU

110
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,720
Bi Dezheng, that's Zheng Yu's phone.
Bring it to her.

111
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:29,400
You bring it to her.

112
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:35,880
It's not that I don't want to.
She went to the restroom.

113
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,160
Just wait.

114
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:39,760
I'm going to get my food delivery.

115
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:47,920
ZHENG YU

116
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:51,920
Could it be the hospital?

117
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,760
<i>Zheng Yu, are you on campus?</i>

118
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:03,560
<i>Two thugs are at the convenience store</i>
<i>asking around for you.</i>

119
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:04,720
<i>They want money from you.</i>

120
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:07,880
<i>They're at the entrance.</i>
<i>I'm telling you, be careful.</i>

121
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,680
What's up?

122
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:18,560
Could she leave from another entrance?

123
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:20,000
Let's keep looking.

124
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:35,600
Who are you?

125
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:36,520
Wait.

126
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:41,240
I remember you.
I saw you at the hospital ward.

127
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,520
We meet again.

128
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:44,880
Perfect.

129
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:46,280
Where is Zheng Yu?

130
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:49,920
Let's cut to the chase.
What will it take for you to leave?

131
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:59,520
<i>Two guys who look like debt collectors</i>
<i>are heading to campus.</i>

132
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:01,280
<i>Got it.</i>

133
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,000
<i>Your classmate answered my call.</i>

134
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:03,920
<i>Did you see him?</i>

135
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:07,040
LU SIQUAN (STORE MANAGER)

136
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:09,160
<i>Not yet.</i>

137
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:13,800
- Where are they?
- Gone.

138
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,600
Gone?

139
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:19,760
They haven't even seen me,

140
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:20,960
and they just left?

141
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:22,600
What did you say?

142
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:25,680
Nothing much.

143
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:28,920
<i>With a guy spending money on you,</i>

144
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:33,040
<i>will you be paying off your debt</i>
<i>faster now?</i>

145
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:34,200
You gave them money?

146
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:39,440
How much?

147
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:43,720
How much?

148
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,760
Ten thousand yuan.

149
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:53,720
I don't have that much right now.

150
00:11:54,320 --> 00:11:56,400
I get paid next week
for a translation gig.

151
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:58,080
Altogether, I'll have…

152
00:11:58,160 --> 00:11:59,800
Don't send it to me.

153
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:03,560
Save it for later.

154
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:09,520
When is later?

155
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:11,920
When I pay off my debt,

156
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:14,640
or when I don't have hospital bills?

157
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:24,800
I'll send this much for now.

158
00:12:25,640 --> 00:12:27,320
Do you have to be like this?

159
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,600
Do you know why I pretended
to have blacked out?

160
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:38,880
Because at some point,

161
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:42,480
my self-respect seemed to have returned.

162
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,800
But I drank alcohol that day

163
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:50,320
and did things
that compromised my self-respect.

164
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:54,000
I really regret it.

165
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:56,600
So I want to forget it.

166
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:23,680
<i>Contact me if there are any gigs.</i>

167
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:24,840
PART-TIME JOB GROUP

168
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:26,720
GIG CONNECTIONS, GIGS FOR FRIENDS

169
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:34,120
<i>Because at some point,</i>

170
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:37,480
<i>my self-respect seemed to have returned.</i>

171
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:40,480
<i>But I drank alcohol that day</i>

172
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:43,120
<i>and did things</i>
<i>that compromised my self-respect.</i>

173
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,440
<i>I really regret it.</i>

174
00:14:45,520 --> 00:14:46,840
<i>So I want to forget it.</i>

175
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:10,640
You're back.

176
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:18,360
Mom, doing a big cleanout?

177
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,200
No.

178
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:24,600
In the community across from us,
I met a cleaning lady.

179
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:26,560
She likes to collect junk to sell.

180
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:28,920
I thought I could give her some.

181
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:32,160
Do you need my help?

182
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:33,400
No.

183
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:36,240
But here are some of your books.

184
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:37,560
See if you want them.

185
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:42,200
Those are from senior high school.
They are no longer of use.

186
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,480
Okay.

187
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:45,120
There are also these.

188
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:46,680
I saw them in your study.

189
00:15:46,760 --> 00:15:49,480
There was a thick layer of dust.

190
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:53,600
But they look like college textbooks.

191
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:54,520
Look.

192
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:55,720
FUNDAMENTALS OF BIOMEDICINE

193
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:57,800
Do you use these books in Life Sciences?

194
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:02,320
I was bored and bought them for fun.

195
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:04,080
I don't need them.

196
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:07,000
Okay.

197
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:08,720
I'll give them away.

198
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:12,000
If that's all, I'm going to go, Mom.

199
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:13,240
Okay.

200
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:16,720
Yanzhou.

201
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:20,440
It's your birthday soon.
How do you want to spend it?

202
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:22,040
My birthday?

203
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:28,320
The same as usual. Just dinner at home.

204
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:31,040
Okay. I'll get your dad to buy a big cake.

205
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:35,360
I remember your wish last year
was to finish your thesis.

206
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:37,400
It has come true, right?

207
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:42,360
Wonderful. Make more wishes
this year. It really works.

208
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:55,040
<i>Directly rejected?</i>

209
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:57,080
Didn't the editor ask you to edit it?

210
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:00,080
No.

211
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:05,920
I should've warned you when you wanted
to submit to <i>Molecular Plant.</i>

212
00:17:07,119 --> 00:17:08,760
Even for graduate students,

213
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:11,480
the chances of getting published are low.

214
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:15,960
Why don't you try again
with a publisher with a lower threshold?

215
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:18,000
If it doesn't pass, let's just give up.

216
00:17:21,599 --> 00:17:24,520
This direction of research
was your brother's interest.

217
00:17:25,119 --> 00:17:26,920
But so much time has passed.

218
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,480
I think you should…

219
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:30,120
I came to tell you

220
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:33,320
that I will continue to revise
and resubmit.

221
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:35,480
I will also send the editor
an explanation.

222
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:38,640
Do you know how slim the chances are

223
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:40,400
for a rejected paper

224
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:42,520
that is resubmitted to the same journal?

225
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:43,440
I know.

226
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:54,960
Why are you so late today?

227
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:57,120
Zheng Yu came in early.

228
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,360
She just left.

229
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:06,840
Did you two agree
to take different shifts?

230
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:27,120
Dezheng, you've been quite diligent
with your experiments.

231
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:30,520
Divorce is looming.

232
00:18:31,120 --> 00:18:33,240
It's up to me
to hold this family together.

233
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,680
Carry on.

234
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:45,920
Divorce?

235
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,560
Hello?

236
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:06,200
<i>Ms. Zheng, you don't have to</i>
<i>come to tutor me today.</i>

237
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:08,480
Why the sudden cancelation?

238
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:12,080
I heard your mom will be back tomorrow.
What if I tell on you?

239
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:13,600
I'm innocent!

240
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:16,520
I'm busy tonight.
Yanzhou is celebrating his birthday.

241
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:18,440
<i>My uncle and aunt called me over.</i>

242
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:20,400
<i>I have to show up.</i>

243
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:21,920
<i>Chen Huimei knows about this.</i>

244
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:24,840
<i>All right, I have to go now.</i>

245
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:26,880
<i>That's all. Don't waste your time coming.</i>

246
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,320
Birthday?

247
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:45,840
Why are you staring at me?

248
00:19:46,440 --> 00:19:48,400
Who were you lost in conversation with?

249
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:50,520
Ms. Zheng.

250
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:53,760
She…

251
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:56,520
Is she almost here?

252
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:00,760
Don't you have tutoring today?

253
00:20:01,480 --> 00:20:04,280
Yanzhou, I came
to celebrate your birthday today.

254
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:05,480
Did you forget?

255
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:09,000
I nearly forgot.

256
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:10,160
Tutoring?

257
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:13,440
You will lose your only cousin
if I die from exhaustion.

258
00:20:14,560 --> 00:20:17,240
Does that mean
Ms. Zheng isn't coming today?

259
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:19,320
Of course not. Duh.

260
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:36,960
CHEN YANZHOU

261
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:41,560
Zheng Yu, don't you have tutoring today?

262
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:42,880
Why haven't you left yet?

263
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:44,480
It was canceled at the last minute.

264
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:53,600
What's up, Zheng Yu?

265
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:55,400
What's on your mind?

266
00:20:57,680 --> 00:21:00,800
A few days ago,
I said some harsh things to a friend.

267
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:02,800
It's their birthday today.

268
00:21:02,880 --> 00:21:06,200
Do you think I should still
wish them a happy birthday?

269
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:10,480
Why not?

270
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:12,880
If you still think of them as a friend,

271
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:15,400
you can take this chance
to bury the hatchet.

272
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:17,720
Maybe

273
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:20,000
they don't want my well-wishes.

274
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:22,240
Maybe they're waiting for them.

275
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:25,320
How will you know the answer
if you don't offer any?

276
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:32,320
I have to go out for something.

277
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:45,440
The final dish.

278
00:21:45,520 --> 00:21:46,680
We can dig in now.

279
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:49,840
<i>Even if you care about your sick mom,</i>

280
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,560
<i>you shouldn't treat yourself this way.</i>

281
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:03,680
Mom.

282
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:07,360
I don't like scrambled eggs
with tomatoes now.

283
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:10,200
Didn't you still like it not long ago?

284
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:13,640
People's preferences can change.

285
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:16,920
I can share my preferences, right?

286
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:21,160
- Of course.
- Yanzhou, just place it over here.

287
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:22,480
It's no big deal.

288
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:26,280
When can we cut the cake?

289
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:28,680
You're such a glutton.

290
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:35,320
- I'll turn off the light.
- Okay.

291
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:41,520
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

292
00:22:41,600 --> 00:22:44,960
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

293
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:48,640
<i>Happy birthday, happy birthday</i>

294
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:52,240
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

295
00:22:53,040 --> 00:22:54,040
Make a wish.

296
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:01,440
I'll turn on the light.

297
00:23:05,640 --> 00:23:06,680
I'll get the door.

298
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:11,600
Grandma?

299
00:23:11,680 --> 00:23:13,880
Are you here
to celebrate Yanzhou's birthday?

300
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:14,960
Mom.

301
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:18,000
The mangoes were picked
too early last time.

302
00:23:18,080 --> 00:23:21,040
This time, they're not bad.
One batch per family.

303
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:24,120
Mom.

304
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:27,440
Since you're here,
sit and join us for dinner.

305
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:33,760
I can't stomach this dinner.

306
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:45,560
Come here.

307
00:23:45,640 --> 00:23:47,040
Come. It's okay.

308
00:23:50,120 --> 00:23:52,080
Grandma, it's late.

309
00:23:52,160 --> 00:23:53,240
It's a long way back.

310
00:23:53,320 --> 00:23:55,920
Why don't you stay for the night?

311
00:23:56,520 --> 00:23:58,800
Besides, my aunt will be back tomorrow.

312
00:23:58,880 --> 00:24:00,680
You haven't seen her lately, right?

313
00:24:00,760 --> 00:24:01,680
Yanzhou,

314
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:04,120
you don't need to be so considerate.

315
00:24:06,240 --> 00:24:07,440
It's nothing.

316
00:24:09,440 --> 00:24:10,880
I'll just ask you this.

317
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:12,960
Is it your birthday today?

318
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:15,680
You don't have to celebrate

319
00:24:15,760 --> 00:24:18,160
this fake birthday every year
just for your mom.

320
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:22,440
It's just celebrating two days early.

321
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:24,480
As you know,

322
00:24:25,480 --> 00:24:26,840
my birthday

323
00:24:27,680 --> 00:24:29,360
is the day my brother passed away.

324
00:24:35,160 --> 00:24:36,040
I know.

325
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:38,440
The past

326
00:24:38,520 --> 00:24:40,320
cannot be changed.

327
00:24:42,560 --> 00:24:45,840
So shouldn't we live our lives
the way we're meant to?

328
00:24:45,920 --> 00:24:47,960
Why does a family need to pretend?

329
00:24:48,840 --> 00:24:50,560
You are so hard on yourself.

330
00:24:50,640 --> 00:24:52,120
Your mom has no idea.

331
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:53,400
She doesn't know

332
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:55,960
and won't appreciate it.

333
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:00,640
I don't need her to appreciate it

334
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:03,920
as long as she is happy.

335
00:25:10,320 --> 00:25:13,440
If you don't want to stay,
I'll take you to a nearby hotel.

336
00:25:57,760 --> 00:26:00,440
Gao Xing was supposed to have
a tutoring session today.

337
00:26:01,880 --> 00:26:03,240
She said she canceled it.

338
00:26:04,600 --> 00:26:07,920
The next session is next week.

339
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:08,840
I'm…

340
00:26:09,520 --> 00:26:12,080
worried she will slack off,
so I brought homework.

341
00:26:14,440 --> 00:26:15,320
Give it to me.

342
00:26:35,640 --> 00:26:36,920
Is this it?

343
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:49,920
Happy birthday.

344
00:26:56,840 --> 00:26:58,120
Nothing's happy about it.

345
00:27:25,680 --> 00:27:26,520
Hey.

346
00:27:32,840 --> 00:27:33,680
Here.

347
00:27:35,480 --> 00:27:38,280
I really forgot it last time.
I'm not that petty.

348
00:27:39,280 --> 00:27:41,880
All right. I'll return it to you
after I make a copy.

349
00:27:42,800 --> 00:27:44,480
Who's the one acting cool now?

350
00:27:49,680 --> 00:27:52,360
Aren't you cold wearing short sleeves
in this weather?

351
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:56,920
Do you think I want to?

352
00:27:57,520 --> 00:28:00,840
I left my jacket at Yanzhou's house
when celebrating his birthday.

353
00:28:00,920 --> 00:28:04,000
It so happens that
we have an open lecture today,

354
00:28:04,080 --> 00:28:05,760
and school uniforms are mandatory.

355
00:28:05,840 --> 00:28:07,040
I have to wear this.

356
00:28:08,680 --> 00:28:11,000
Who are you kidding?
You only have one uniform?

357
00:28:12,440 --> 00:28:15,560
I threw my other set in the trash
in a fight with Chen Huimei.

358
00:28:16,400 --> 00:28:18,000
Chen Huimei?

359
00:28:19,520 --> 00:28:20,360
My mom.

360
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:55,120
It's clean.

361
00:29:00,800 --> 00:29:04,200
I didn't expect this extortionist
to have such a kind side.

362
00:29:05,760 --> 00:29:10,080
I… It's a fair exchange.
I hope you can be nicer to my sister.

363
00:29:16,240 --> 00:29:18,080
I'm super nice to Ms. Zheng.

364
00:29:18,160 --> 00:29:19,840
You can ask her yourself.

365
00:29:19,920 --> 00:29:22,520
Yanzhou too. He's very nice to Ms. Zheng.

366
00:29:22,600 --> 00:29:24,120
Just not quite as nice as me.

367
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:26,200
You probably noticed during that dinner.

368
00:29:26,280 --> 00:29:27,480
He actually…

369
00:29:32,960 --> 00:29:34,000
What?

370
00:29:34,080 --> 00:29:35,920
No taking back what you lent.

371
00:29:36,920 --> 00:29:40,560
Last time, you mentioned that you
and your cousin live in the same area.

372
00:29:41,560 --> 00:29:42,400
Yes.

373
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:45,880
You would rather brave the cold
than go get your jacket.

374
00:29:45,960 --> 00:29:46,840
Did you lie again?

375
00:29:48,280 --> 00:29:50,840
I don't want to go to his house
just for this.

376
00:29:52,160 --> 00:29:53,720
You just praised him.

377
00:29:54,440 --> 00:29:56,760
He is not his house.

378
00:29:59,160 --> 00:30:00,320
Sometimes,

379
00:30:00,400 --> 00:30:01,840
I'm scared of going there.

380
00:30:06,680 --> 00:30:07,760
You wouldn't get it.

381
00:30:19,120 --> 00:30:20,280
Are you going out?

382
00:30:21,280 --> 00:30:22,680
Where to? It's so early.

383
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:29,200
I'm going

384
00:30:29,280 --> 00:30:30,120
to class.

385
00:30:41,120 --> 00:30:42,760
- Pang Wei.
- Here.

386
00:30:44,360 --> 00:30:46,320
- Liu Tianyu.
- Here.

387
00:30:47,800 --> 00:30:49,760
- Xu Fangli.
- Here.

388
00:30:50,960 --> 00:30:52,920
- Zhang Qi.
- Here.

389
00:30:54,040 --> 00:30:55,240
Chen Yanzhou.

390
00:30:56,560 --> 00:30:57,840
Is Chen Yanzhou here?

391
00:31:05,400 --> 00:31:06,520
That's one absence.

392
00:31:06,600 --> 00:31:08,960
If anyone knows him,
please pass the word along.

393
00:31:09,840 --> 00:31:11,600
A top student skipping class?

394
00:31:23,600 --> 00:31:25,960
BELOVED SON ZHOU GUANQI

395
00:31:28,320 --> 00:31:29,360
Looks like

396
00:31:30,200 --> 00:31:31,760
Dad has come here already.

397
00:31:44,960 --> 00:31:46,400
Even if I don't say it,

398
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:48,040
you can probably guess.

399
00:31:49,360 --> 00:31:50,440
My paper didn't pass.

400
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:55,240
The reviewer didn't even tell me
what the problem is.

401
00:31:56,280 --> 00:31:57,320
You're so smart.

402
00:31:57,920 --> 00:31:59,400
If you have time,

403
00:31:59,480 --> 00:32:00,920
can you help?

404
00:32:05,320 --> 00:32:06,680
Never mind.

405
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:09,640
You might be mad after you read it.

406
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:14,160
Mad that I spent so much time

407
00:32:15,400 --> 00:32:17,560
and only got this far.

408
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:23,560
Mom, why did we suddenly come here?

409
00:32:24,560 --> 00:32:27,880
Don't you miss Daddy?
I know, even if you don't tell me.

410
00:32:27,960 --> 00:32:30,400
You can tell me next time.

411
00:32:30,480 --> 00:32:31,720
I don't want to.

412
00:32:31,800 --> 00:32:33,480
No matter what I say,

413
00:32:33,560 --> 00:32:35,480
Daddy won't answer anyway.

414
00:32:37,520 --> 00:32:41,120
But if we don't talk about him
and avoid everything related to him,

415
00:32:41,920 --> 00:32:43,800
it's like he never existed.

416
00:32:43,880 --> 00:32:46,040
That is what is most heartbreaking.

417
00:32:46,120 --> 00:32:49,640
When we miss Daddy,
we can say his name often.

418
00:32:49,720 --> 00:32:53,720
We can also keep talking
about our memories of him.

419
00:32:53,800 --> 00:32:57,440
That way, he'll know that
we haven't forgotten him.

420
00:32:57,520 --> 00:32:59,320
As long as we haven't forgotten him,

421
00:32:59,400 --> 00:33:02,360
he will continue to live in another world.

422
00:33:02,440 --> 00:33:03,680
Got it?

423
00:33:10,800 --> 00:33:12,120
Guanqi.

424
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:16,160
I think it has been a long time

425
00:33:17,400 --> 00:33:19,160
since we've talked about you.

426
00:33:20,280 --> 00:33:22,080
BELOVED SON

427
00:33:30,280 --> 00:33:32,200
CIGARETTES

428
00:33:44,960 --> 00:33:45,800
You're back.

429
00:33:50,480 --> 00:33:51,520
Why aren't you home?

430
00:33:54,720 --> 00:33:56,520
I came to give you this.

431
00:33:58,120 --> 00:33:59,440
After this,

432
00:34:00,360 --> 00:34:01,920
I have to return to the office.

433
00:34:14,360 --> 00:34:15,400
A birthday gift.

434
00:34:17,280 --> 00:34:19,199
Today is your actual birthday.

435
00:34:19,880 --> 00:34:20,920
I think

436
00:34:21,520 --> 00:34:23,320
giving it today is more appropriate.

437
00:34:27,360 --> 00:34:29,000
I wish you a happy birthday.

438
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:48,920
Thank you, Dad.

439
00:35:08,960 --> 00:35:10,160
You're back.

440
00:35:12,960 --> 00:35:16,320
What's the occasion?
How come you bought flowers?

441
00:35:19,160 --> 00:35:21,080
They're from the flower shop nearby.

442
00:35:21,920 --> 00:35:25,640
They're not fresh anymore,
but the owner didn't want to toss them.

443
00:35:25,720 --> 00:35:29,120
So I bought them for a steal.
They should last a few days.

444
00:35:29,200 --> 00:35:30,360
They're nice.

445
00:35:33,760 --> 00:35:36,760
Mom, if there's nothing you need,
I'm going to my room.

446
00:35:37,760 --> 00:35:38,800
Okay.

447
00:35:40,640 --> 00:35:42,960
Right, Yanzhou.

448
00:35:43,960 --> 00:35:45,000
I forgot to say.

449
00:35:53,800 --> 00:35:58,600
Do you remember the lady
I told you about who collects junk?

450
00:36:01,360 --> 00:36:04,800
The one we gave all those old books to.

451
00:36:05,800 --> 00:36:07,720
She was delighted when she got them.

452
00:36:07,800 --> 00:36:11,160
She even invited me to go fruit-picking
at an orchard this weekend.

453
00:36:14,360 --> 00:36:15,200
That's sudden.

454
00:36:15,280 --> 00:36:17,040
Not really.

455
00:36:17,120 --> 00:36:20,080
She's told me before
that her husband works at an orchard

456
00:36:20,160 --> 00:36:23,120
and to go with her when I had time.

457
00:36:23,200 --> 00:36:26,160
She seems to have a tough life,
so I didn't turn her down.

458
00:36:28,960 --> 00:36:30,040
Yanzhou?

459
00:36:34,720 --> 00:36:36,240
Manhuo Orchard, right?

460
00:36:36,320 --> 00:36:38,400
Dad is busy and probably won't have time.

461
00:36:38,480 --> 00:36:39,400
I'll drive you.

462
00:36:39,480 --> 00:36:40,840
You don't have to.

463
00:36:40,920 --> 00:36:43,280
You're busy studying and writing a thesis.

464
00:36:43,360 --> 00:36:46,520
Don't worry. I already agreed
to take the bus with her.

465
00:36:47,160 --> 00:36:48,360
Okay.

466
00:36:49,120 --> 00:36:51,760
The Route 24 bus right outside
should take you there.

467
00:36:51,840 --> 00:36:54,520
I've been there for fieldwork before.

468
00:36:56,080 --> 00:36:57,040
Really?

469
00:36:57,720 --> 00:36:59,080
I see.

470
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:02,160
Is there anything else

471
00:37:03,040 --> 00:37:04,520
you want to say?

472
00:37:05,720 --> 00:37:07,040
No. Go ahead.

473
00:37:08,960 --> 00:37:10,440
Then

474
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:12,280
good night, Mom.

475
00:37:13,320 --> 00:37:14,160
Good night.

476
00:38:04,800 --> 00:38:07,160
<i>A top student skipping class?</i>

477
00:38:17,200 --> 00:38:20,040
CHEN YANZHOU

478
00:38:22,160 --> 00:38:23,280
<i>Happy birthday.</i>

479
00:38:24,720 --> 00:38:26,320
<i>Nothing's happy about it.</i>

480
00:38:38,640 --> 00:38:41,160
QIAN YIWEN

481
00:38:47,960 --> 00:38:49,800
<i>Hello? Is this Zheng Yu?</i>

482
00:38:50,400 --> 00:38:53,200
<i>I heard you've been looking</i>
<i>for part-time gigs again.</i>

483
00:38:53,280 --> 00:38:55,440
<i>I want you for a photoshoot this weekend.</i>

484
00:38:55,520 --> 00:38:56,960
<i>Are you free?</i>

485
00:38:57,760 --> 00:39:00,560
HOUDE HALL

486
00:39:10,680 --> 00:39:13,920
Are you on the day shift,
while she's on the night shift today?

487
00:39:20,080 --> 00:39:23,680
This has been on my mind more than
the experiments in the last few days.

488
00:39:24,280 --> 00:39:25,720
I clearly remember

489
00:39:25,800 --> 00:39:28,760
that the day we went out
to buy a gift for the boss,

490
00:39:28,840 --> 00:39:29,880
you two were fine.

491
00:39:30,480 --> 00:39:32,280
Why did you suddenly have a falling out?

492
00:39:38,640 --> 00:39:41,080
Just be honest. How did you piss her off?

493
00:39:42,080 --> 00:39:43,240
We're a team.

494
00:39:43,320 --> 00:39:44,960
You're a man. Give in to her.

495
00:39:45,040 --> 00:39:46,760
Zheng Yu is quite nice.

496
00:39:47,360 --> 00:39:48,600
I didn't piss her off.

497
00:39:50,720 --> 00:39:51,760
She bullied me.

498
00:39:56,440 --> 00:40:00,080
Zheng Yu should really see
how miserable you look.

499
00:40:00,920 --> 00:40:02,080
She would feel bad.

500
00:40:19,920 --> 00:40:21,080
MS. ZHOU

501
00:40:21,160 --> 00:40:22,960
<i>I'm waiting for the bus.</i>

502
00:40:33,720 --> 00:40:36,080
When my son was 28,

503
00:40:36,160 --> 00:40:38,320
he had an accident at a construction site

504
00:40:38,400 --> 00:40:39,680
and didn't survive.

505
00:40:40,640 --> 00:40:41,520
Over the years,

506
00:40:41,600 --> 00:40:46,000
my husband has worked
at the orchard to support us.

507
00:40:49,040 --> 00:40:50,600
Twenty-eight years old.

508
00:40:51,800 --> 00:40:52,680
So young.

509
00:40:55,520 --> 00:40:57,440
Life and death are predestined.

510
00:40:57,520 --> 00:40:59,760
The young aren't spared from fate.

511
00:41:00,920 --> 00:41:03,720
I have to keep looking forward.

512
00:41:03,800 --> 00:41:07,040
Sometimes, I have dark thoughts too.

513
00:41:07,680 --> 00:41:10,600
So I share what I feel with my family.

514
00:41:10,680 --> 00:41:12,800
Sometimes, saying it out loud

515
00:41:12,880 --> 00:41:14,600
makes you feel lighter.

516
00:41:26,160 --> 00:41:28,960
People should live in the present.

517
00:41:36,320 --> 00:41:39,080
You don't have to adjust anything.
Just use this filter.

518
00:41:39,160 --> 00:41:40,680
This is the shutter.

519
00:41:40,760 --> 00:41:42,320
Just press it once.

520
00:41:42,400 --> 00:41:43,280
It's done.

521
00:41:43,360 --> 00:41:44,680
This is the replay button.

522
00:41:45,720 --> 00:41:48,320
That's all. Just pay attention
to the composition.

523
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:51,120
Are we just going there to take photos?

524
00:41:52,200 --> 00:41:54,000
Is it weird that I asked you along?

525
00:41:55,160 --> 00:41:56,240
A bit.

526
00:41:56,320 --> 00:41:58,680
I just want someone to take photos for me.

527
00:41:58,760 --> 00:42:00,320
The others don't like doing it.

528
00:42:00,400 --> 00:42:03,160
If I invited them
and kept asking them to take photos,

529
00:42:03,240 --> 00:42:04,240
I would feel bad.

530
00:42:04,320 --> 00:42:06,920
So it's better to ask a stranger.

531
00:42:07,880 --> 00:42:08,880
I sort of get it.

532
00:42:09,840 --> 00:42:11,760
Manhuo Orchard is still ages away.

533
00:42:11,840 --> 00:42:13,080
You can take a nap.

534
00:42:13,160 --> 00:42:14,680
You have serious dark circles.

535
00:42:28,680 --> 00:42:31,000
Chen Yanzhou, let's grab a bite.

536
00:42:31,080 --> 00:42:32,680
No. I have no appetite.

537
00:42:35,360 --> 00:42:39,000
I'll go with you. I'm starving.
He's busy later. Right?

538
00:42:41,720 --> 00:42:42,680
Let's go.

539
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:51,360
MS. ZHOU
I'M WAITING FOR THE BUS.

540
00:42:53,000 --> 00:42:54,760
<i>I was working on experiments.</i>

541
00:42:55,600 --> 00:42:57,720
<i>Is the trip going well?</i>

542
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:12,840
Hello.

543
00:43:13,440 --> 00:43:14,600
Mom, where are you now?

544
00:43:16,120 --> 00:43:17,960
Just past Innovation Industrial Park.

545
00:43:20,080 --> 00:43:21,520
You didn't reply to my text.

546
00:43:21,600 --> 00:43:23,720
I called just in case
you missed your stop.

547
00:43:24,920 --> 00:43:26,200
I don't go out often,

548
00:43:26,280 --> 00:43:28,960
but I know how to read bus stop signs.

549
00:43:29,040 --> 00:43:30,160
<i>What if you dozed off?</i>

550
00:43:32,680 --> 00:43:34,480
That is possible.

551
00:43:36,400 --> 00:43:39,680
I used to always look down, volunteering
and picking up trash with everyone.

552
00:43:40,560 --> 00:43:43,640
<i>Now I've realized that our city</i>
<i>is very beautiful.</i>

553
00:43:43,720 --> 00:43:45,600
<i>It's so scenic.</i>

554
00:43:46,320 --> 00:43:48,360
If you like it, I'll tell Dad.

555
00:43:48,440 --> 00:43:49,600
In the future,

556
00:43:50,560 --> 00:43:51,800
we can go out more often.

557
00:43:52,400 --> 00:43:53,320
Sure.

558
00:43:53,960 --> 00:43:55,680
Let's all go out together.

559
00:43:57,480 --> 00:43:59,240
<i>By the way, have you eaten yet?</i>

560
00:43:59,320 --> 00:44:00,840
Doing experiments is tiring,

561
00:44:00,920 --> 00:44:02,840
but don't forget to eat.

562
00:44:04,800 --> 00:44:05,720
Hello?

563
00:44:06,760 --> 00:44:07,680
Hello?
